        "comment": "expanded from 20th Century Studios, the production notes, Variety and Box Office Mojo",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Meryl Streep, in Disney's production notes: Stanley Tucci \"is married to Emily's sister. It's all very nepotistic!\"}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = The Devil Wears Prada 2\n| directed by = David Frankel\n| written by = Aline Brosh McKenna\n| theatrical release = 1 May 2026\n| rating = PG-13\n| runtime = 1 hour 59 minutes\n| worldwide gross, 8 October 2026 = $693,255,651\n| script changes = none, according to the director\n}}\n\n'''The Devil Wears Prada 2''' is a 2026 comedy-drama directed by David Frankel and written by Aline Brosh McKenna, released theatrically on 1 May 2026 by 20th Century Studios.<ref name=\"studio\">\"The Devil Wears Prada 2\", 20th Century Studios. https://www.20thcenturystudios.com/movies/the-devil-wears-prada-2</ref> By 8 October 2026 it was on Disney+ and Hulu, and for sale on Blu-ray and digital.<ref name=\"studio\" /> Frankel says the studio did not change a word of the script. Streep's note on the cast was that it was all very nepotistic.<ref name=\"notes\">\"The Devil Wears Prada 2\" production notes, 20th Century Studios / Disney. https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/dwp2_localised_production_notes_dc3051c8.pdf</ref>\n\n== The same people ==\nThe studio page says the film \"reunites the original main cast with director David Frankel and writer Aline Brosh McKenna.\" It is rated PG-13, runs 1 hour 59 minutes, and is filed under comedy and drama, with the release date 1 May 2026.<ref name=\"studio\" /> Returning names on that page include Meryl Streep, Anne Hathaway, Emily Blunt, Stanley Tucci, Tracie Thoms as Lily, and Tibor Feldman as Irv. New names include Kenneth Branagh, Simone Ashley, Justin Theroux, Lucy Liu, Patrick Brammall, Caleb Hearon, Helen J. Shen, Pauline Chalamet, B.J. Novak, and Conrad Ricamora.<ref name=\"studio\" />\n\nThe production notes credit it as \"Based Upon the Characters Created by: Lauren Weisberger,\" with Florian Ballhaus as director of photography, Theodore Shapiro as composer, and Molly Rogers as costume designer.<ref name=\"notes\" /> Frankel says he kept a journal on the 2006 shoot, and that \"The studio loved the script. Didn't change a word.\"<ref name=\"notes\" />\n\n== Where the characters went ==\nVariety's account, published 30 July 2026, places Andy Sachs as the magazine's features editor and Emily Charlton as \"a high-powered executive at Dior\" who controls advertising money ''Runway'' needs after a scandal.<ref name=\"var\">\"Devil Wears Prada 2 Sets Disney+ Streaming Release Date\", ''Variety'', 30 July 2026. https://variety.com/2026/film/news/devil-wears-prada-2-disney-plus-streaming-release-date-1236757274/</ref> The same story lists on-screen appearances by Ashley Graham, Donatella Versace, Lady Gaga, Kara Swisher, Jenna Bush Hager, Paige DeSorbo, Hannah Berner, and Tina Brown.<ref name=\"var\" />\n\nThe notes give character names the cast list does not: Justin Theroux as Benji Barnes, Lucy Liu as Sasha Barnes, Kenneth Branagh as Stuart, B.J. Novak as Jay Ravitz, Simone Ashley as Amari, Patrick Brammall as Peter, Caleb Hearon as Charlie, Helen J. Shen as Jin.<ref name=\"notes\" /> Streep's line in those notes is about Tucci, who \"played my husband in 'Julie & Julia'\" and, in the sequel, \"is married to Emily's sister. It's all very nepotistic!\"<ref name=\"notes\" />\n\n== The gross ==\nBox Office Mojo, opened 8 October 2026, listed a domestic gross of $220,556,651, international $472,699,000, and worldwide $693,255,651. The domestic opening was $76,747,075. The distributor is Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures. The earliest listed release is 29 April 2026, in France, Switzerland, Belgium, Bulgaria, South Korea, Taiwan, the Philippines, Hong Kong, and Indonesia. Italy's opening, $13,432,637 on 30 April, was larger than the United Kingdom's $12,646,000 on 1 May.<ref name=\"mojo\">\"The Devil Wears Prada 2\", Box Office Mojo. https://www.boxofficemojo.com/title/tt33612209/</ref>\n\nVariety, on 30 July, had the worldwide figure at $677 million, and said the film was then \"officially available\" to stream.<ref name=\"var\" /> The studio page's own line, later, was: \"NOW STREAMING ON DISNEY+ AND HULU. BUY IT NOW ON BLU-RAY AND DIGITAL.\"<ref name=\"studio\" /> No studio budget was on the pages opened for this article.\n\nThe studio did not change a word. Streep counted the marriages anyway.\n\n== The opening weekend ==\nThe Walt Disney Company, on 3 May 2026, said the film \"grossed an estimated $233.6 million worldwide in its opening weekend, including $77 million domestically and $156.6 million internationally.\" It said that opening was \"the highest opening weekend ever for Meryl Streep across domestic, international, and global markets,\" and that the sequel had already made 72 percent of the original film's $326 million global total.<ref name=\"disney\">\"'The Devil Wears Prada 2' Delivers One of 2026's Biggest Global Openings\", The Walt Disney Company, 3 May 2026. https://thewaltdisneycompany.com/news/devil-wears-prada-2-box-office/</ref> The same release quoted Frankel: \"It's not nostalgia. It's curiosity.\" It quoted McKenna: \"It's not meant to just be a love letter to the fans.\"\n\nDeadline's Sunday-morning account the same day had the U.S. figure at $77 million and the worldwide opening at $233.6 million, and said the picture \"literally began filming last July.\"<ref name=\"deadline\">Anthony D'Alessandro, \"The Devil Wears Prada 2 Stunning With $233M+ WW Opening\", ''Deadline'', 3 May 2026. https://deadline.com/2026/05/box-office-devil-wears-prada-2-michael-1236877817/</ref> Those are opening estimates. Box Office Mojo's later total, read on 8 October 2026, is the $693,255,651.\n\nThe studio did not change a word of the script. The opening weekend was $233.6 million, and Streep still called the cast list nepotistic.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
