        "comment": "expanded from Britannica, Billboard, CBS, Newsweek, the Guardian and the BBC",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Madonna, after the 2015 Brit Awards, to ''The Guardian'': \"I could either be strangled or fall, and I chose to fall.\"}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Madonna\n| born = 16 August 1958, Bay City, Michigan\n| birth name = Madonna Louise Veronica Ciccone\n| 1984 entrance = a 17-foot wedding cake\n| Sex book, first day = 150,000 copies, at $49.95, in a Mylar bag\n| 2015 cape = Armani, tied too tight; she chose to fall\n| 2023 = a several-day ICU stay, per her manager\n| Confessions II = her 10th album to top the U.S. charts, per Britannica, 2026\n}}\n\n'''Madonna''' is an American singer and actress, born Madonna Louise Veronica Ciccone on 16 August 1958 in Bay City, Michigan.<ref name=\"brit\">\"Madonna\", ''Encyclopaedia Britannica'', revised 27 September 2026. https://www.britannica.com/biography/Madonna-American-singer-and-actress</ref> On 14 September 1984 she came out of a 17-foot wedding cake. In 2015 an Armani cape was tied too tight, and she said she chose to fall rather than be strangled.<ref name=\"bill\">\"Madonna's 1984 MTV VMAs Performance\", ''Billboard''. https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/madonna-1984-mtv-vmas-performance-6296887/</ref><ref name=\"britawards\">\"Madonna suffered whiplash falling off Brits stage\", ''The Guardian'', 27 February 2015. https://www.theguardian.com/music/2015/feb/27/madonna-suffered-whiplash-falling-brits-stage-o2-armani-cape</ref>\n\n== The cake ==\nThe first MTV Video Music Awards were broadcast on 14 September 1984. A Bengal tiger was refused. She emerged from a 17-foot wedding cake in a white wedding dress. She later said, \"I'll just pretend I meant to do this,\" and that \"the underpants were showing.\"<ref name=\"bill\" /> On ''American Bandstand'' that year, Britannica records, she said she wanted \"to rule the world.\"<ref name=\"brit\" />\n\n== The commercial and the book ==\nIn 1989 Pepsi pulled a commercial. On 19 September 2023 she wrote on Instagram, as CBS News quoted it: \"The commercial was immediately canceled when I refused to change any scenes in the video where I was kissing a black saint or burning crosses.\"<ref name=\"cbs\">\"Madonna says her 1989 Pepsi commercial was canceled when she refused to change scenes\", CBS News, 19 September 2023. https://www.cbsnews.com/news/madonna-pepsi-commercial-canceled-1989-like-a-prayer/</ref>\n\nIn 1992 she published ''Sex'', which Britannica calls \"a soft-core pornographic coffee-table book,\" released with the album ''Erotica''.<ref name=\"brit\" /> ''Newsweek'', on 1 November 1992, priced it at \"$49.95\" and said it was \"packaged in a Mylar bag that warned ADULTs ONLY!\" It \"sold 150,000 copies on the first day, out of 500,000 printed for American distribution.\" Warner Books president Laurence J. Kirshbaum called it \"reviewproof.\"<ref name=\"nw\">\"Madonna's 'Sex' Book: The New Voyeurism\", ''Newsweek'', 1 November 1992. https://www.newsweek.com/madonnas-sex-book-new-voyeurism-196758</ref> A bag, a price, and a word stamped on the bag. The reviews were optional.\n\n== The cape ==\nAt the Brit Awards on 25 February 2015 she fell on the stage at the O2. ''The Guardian'' reported that she \"suffered whiplash\" and that the \"Armani cape was tied too tight.\" Her account: \"I could either be strangled or fall, and I chose to fall.\" She also said, \"No more capes.\"<ref name=\"britawards\" />\n\n== 2023, and after ==\nOn 28 June 2023 the BBC reported that her manager, Guy Oseary, said she had developed a \"serious bacterial infection\" on Saturday 24 June, which led to \"a several day stay in the ICU.\" The Celebration Tour, due to start in Vancouver on 15 July, would be paused.<ref name=\"bbc\">\"Madonna postpones tour after stay in intensive care\", BBC, 28 June 2023. https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-us-canada-66049222</ref> That is his account of a hospitalization, not a diagnosis added later.\n\nBritannica, revised 27 September 2026, says the Celebration Tour wrapped in Rio de Janeiro in May 2024 with a free concert on the beach attended by 1.6 million people, and that ''Confessions II'' (2026) \"became the 10th album of her career to top the U.S. charts.\"<ref name=\"brit\" /> The Rio figure is Britannica's. A separate audit was not opened for this article.\n\nShe came out of a 17-foot cake. At the Brits she chose to fall.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Musicians]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
