        "comment": "expanded from the Nintendo releases and the Mojo rankings page",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Nintendo, 10 March 2026: Donald Glover will voice Yoshi in all languages and territories worldwide.}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = The Super Mario Galaxy Movie\n| U.S. release = 1 April 2026\n| Japan release = 24 April 2026\n| worldwide gross, Mojo rankings page = $1,012,608,467\n| budget, Mojo rankings page = $110,000,000\n| Yoshi, all languages = Donald Glover\n}}\n\n'''The Super Mario Galaxy Movie''' is a 2026 animated film. Nintendo and Illumination set the U.S. date, and the date for many other markets, at 1 April 2026, and set Japan at 24 April 2026. Universal Pictures is the worldwide distributor. The film is co-financed by Universal and Nintendo.<ref name=\"jan\">Nintendo release with Illumination, 25 January 2026. https://www.nintendo.co.jp/corporate/release/en/2026/260125.html</ref> As of 8 October 2026 it had been released. A streaming date was not confirmed on the pages opened. No page opened said whether any prints were still in theaters on 8 October 2026.<ref name=\"jan\" />\n\nThe 25 January release moved the U.S. date from 3 April 2026 to 1 April 2026. Japan stayed 24 April 2026. The sentence is \"will move from April 3, 2026 to April 1, 2026 in the US.\"<ref name=\"jan\" />\n\n== The 2023 film and the crew ==\nThat release says both this film and the 2023 film The Super Mario Bros. Movie are produced by Chris Meledandri and Shigeru Miyamoto. It says the 2023 film \"earned more than $1.3 billion worldwide.\" The directors are Aaron Horvath and Michael Jelenic, \"returning filmmakers.\" The screenplay is by Matthew Fogel. The score is by Brian Tyler.<ref name=\"jan2\">Nintendo, 25 January 2026, on the producers, the directors, and the 2023 gross. https://www.nintendo.co.jp/corporate/release/en/2026/260125.html</ref>\n\n== The voices ==\nThe voice cast on the 25 January release is Chris Pratt as Mario, Anya Taylor-Joy as Princess Peach, Charlie Day as Luigi, Jack Black as Bowser, Keegan-Michael Key as Toad, Benny Safdie as Bowser Jr., Kevin Michael Richardson as Kamek, and Brie Larson as Rosalina.<ref name=\"cast\">Nintendo, 25 January 2026, the voice cast. https://www.nintendo.co.jp/corporate/release/en/2026/260125.html</ref>\n\nA Nintendo release of 10 March 2026, issued during a Nintendo Direct, adds Yoshi, Honey Queen, and Wart, and repeats the 1 April and 24 April dates. The sentence is \"Donald Glover will voice Yoshi in all languages and territories worldwide.\"<ref name=\"march\">Nintendo release, 10 March 2026. https://www.nintendo.co.jp/corporate/release/en/2026/260310.html</ref> The same release names Issa Rae as Honey Queen and Luis Guzmán as Wart. It says related material would run on the Nintendo Today! app, which requires a free Nintendo Account.<ref name=\"march2\">Nintendo, 10 March 2026, on Honey Queen, Wart, and the app. https://www.nintendo.co.jp/corporate/release/en/2026/260310.html</ref> WebFetch timed out twice on that 10 March URL. The text here is from a successful curl of the same URL.<ref name=\"march2\" />\n\n== 1889 and the hanafuda cards ==\nIllumination blurb on that page says the company was founded by Chris Meledandri in 2007 and that its films \"have grossed nearly $11 billion worldwide.\" Nintendo blurb says the company was founded in 1889, \"beginning with the manufacture and sale of Hanafuda playing cards,\" and has sold more than 6 billion video games and over 870 million hardware units.<ref name=\"hana\">Nintendo, 10 March 2026, the company blurbs. https://www.nintendo.co.jp/corporate/release/en/2026/260310.html</ref>\n\n== The rankings page ==\nBox Office Mojo rankings page lists distributor Universal Pictures, release 1 April 2026, MPAA PG, running time 1 hr 38 min, opening $131,703,340 in 4,252 theaters, widest release 4,284 theaters, and budget $110,000,000.<ref name=\"rank\">Box Office Mojo rankings page. https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl3344662529/rankings/</ref> On that same page the grosses were domestic $429,814,610 (42.4 percent), international $582,793,857 (57.6 percent), and worldwide $1,012,608,467.<ref name=\"rank2\">Box Office Mojo rankings page, the gross lines. https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl3344662529/rankings/</ref>\n\nDuring the same research session, other Mojo subpages showed worldwide totals of $1,012,578,077 and $1,012,751,766. The figure used here is only the rankings page. The other two totals are what those subpages showed. They are not substituted for the rankings-page gross.<ref name=\"rank2\" /> A May 2026 streaming date on a Rotten Tomatoes search snippet was not opened.\n\nThe January release names eight voices. Pratt, Taylor-Joy, Day, Black, Key, Safdie, Richardson, and Larson are that list. The March release adds Glover, Rae, and Guzmán. One March sentence covers every language and every territory for Yoshi. The same page gives Nintendo a start in 1889 with hanafuda cards, then more than 6 billion video games and over 870 million hardware units, and gives Illumination, founded by Meledandri in 2007, a film total of nearly $11 billion. The opening theater count on the rankings page is 4252.\n\nDonald Glover voices Yoshi in all languages. The company dates its founding to 1889 and to hanafuda cards.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
