        "user": "CubeWatch",
        "daysAgo": 7,
        "comment": "expanded from Britannica, the Los Angeles Times, Time, Variety, USA Today, Rolling Stone, the Walk of Fame and Billboard",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=USA Today, 29 November 2018, on the middle-name poll: the options included TheMcRibIsBack. Rolling Stone, 25 November 2025, reporting his statement: \"My name is Macaulay Macaulay Culkin Culkin.\"}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Macaulay Culkin\n| born = 26 August 1980, New York City\n| Home Alone fee, reported = $250,000\n| worldwide gross, Variety = $476 million\n| Walk of Fame = 1 December 2023, the 2,765th star\n| name he states = Macaulay Macaulay Culkin Culkin\n}}\n\n'''Macaulay Culkin''' was born on 26 August 1980 in New York City.<ref name=\"brit\">Encyclopaedia Britannica, \"Macaulay Culkin,\" revised 14 September 2026. https://www.britannica.com/biography/Macaulay-Culkin</ref> The fee printed for the first ''Home Alone'' is a reported figure, not a studio document. The name he gives in 2025 is Macaulay Macaulay Culkin Culkin. Bunny Ears is a website. The band was the Pizza Underground.\n\n== The reported fee ==\nThe ''Los Angeles Times'', on 12 May 1991, wrote: \"For his role in the original film, Culkin was paid a reported $250,000.\" ''Time'' the same season: \"Culkin, who was paid only $250,000 for Home Alone.\"<ref name=\"lat\">''Los Angeles Times'', 12 May 1991. https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1991-05-12-ca-2329-story.html</ref><ref name=\"time\">''Time'', \"At Home but Not Alone.\" https://time.com/archive/6719146/at-home-but-not-alone/</ref> Variety, on 1 December 2023, wrote that the film \"grossed $476 million worldwide.\"<ref name=\"var\">Variety, 1 December 2023. https://variety.com/2023/film/features/macaulay-culkin-walk-of-fame-childhood-fame-1235815634/</ref> A widely repeated fee of $100,000 was not on the ''Times'', ''Time'', or Variety pages opened for this article. The reported original fee in the Los Angeles Times is $250,000.\n\nThe sequel price is also a report. The ''Times'' said \"reportedly $4.5 million, plus 5% of the gross.\" A Fox spokeswoman said a deal was signed, \"but not exactly for those terms.\" By that week the first film had sold \"$267.5 million\" in the United States and \"$140 million\" overseas.<ref name=\"latseq\">''Los Angeles Times'', 12 May 1991, on the sequel terms and the gross then in hand. https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1991-05-12-ca-2329-story.html</ref> ''Time'' placed ''Home Alone'', at that point, as \"the third highest grossing movie of all time. (Only E.T. and Star Wars have made more money.)\"<ref name=\"timegross\">''Time'' on the early gross ranking. https://time.com/archive/6719146/at-home-but-not-alone/</ref>\n\n== The poll ==\nUSA Today, on 29 November 2018, reported a poll on his site BunnyEars. He called it \"Goop meets The Onion a little bit.\" The middle name then was Carson. The five options were \"Macaulay Culkin, Shark Week, Kieran, TheMcRibIsBack and Publicity Stunt.\"<ref name=\"usa\">USA Today, 29 November 2018. https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/entertainthis/2018/11/29/macaulay-culkin-poll-bunnyears-jimmy-fallon-tonight-show/2147348002/</ref> Rolling Stone, on 25 November 2025, reported his statement: \"My name is Macaulay Macaulay Culkin Culkin.\" The same story says he \"legally changed his name in 2019.\"<ref name=\"rs\">''Rolling Stone'', 25 November 2025. https://www.rollingstone.com/tv-movies/tv-movie-news/macaulay-culkin-legally-changed-name-2018-poll-1235472467/</ref> That is his public statement, as Rolling Stone reported it. A court file was not opened.\n\n== The site and the band ==\nThe Hollywood Walk of Fame press release calls Bunny Ears the \"new media empire\" he founded, \"a Podcast website, live events as well as social and merchandising components.\"<ref name=\"wof\">Hollywood Walk of Fame press release. https://walkoffame.com/press_releases/macaulay-culkin-celebrates-40-year-acting-career-with-star-on-the-hollywood-walk-of-fame/</ref> Britannica says the band was another thing: \"He formed a band called the Pizza Underground\" that \"went on a brief tour in 2014,\" Velvet Underground covers with pizza lyrics. Bunny Ears, the comedy site and podcast, launched in 2017.<ref name=\"britband\">Encyclopaedia Britannica on the Pizza Underground and on Bunny Ears. https://www.britannica.com/biography/Macaulay-Culkin</ref> The website is not the band.\n\n== The star and the advertisement ==\nThe Chamber's release places the star as the 2,765th, on Friday 1 December at 11:30 a.m., in the category Motion Pictures, with speakers Catherine O'Hara and Natasha Lyonne.<ref name=\"wofdate\">Walk of Fame release on the star number, the hour, and the speakers. https://walkoffame.com/press_releases/macaulay-culkin-celebrates-40-year-acting-career-with-star-on-the-hollywood-walk-of-fame/</ref> Variety that morning, 1 December 2023, previewed the ceremony and printed the $476 million gross.<ref name=\"var\" /> The Google item from the notes is not a Doodle. Billboard, on 19 December 2018, described a Google Assistant commercial, \"a shot-for-shot remake of scenes from the Christmas classic,\" dropped that Wednesday, while he was promoting \"his website and podcast, Bunny Ears.\"<ref name=\"bb\">Billboard, 19 December 2018. https://www.billboard.com/pro/macaulay-culkin-re-creates-home-alone-scenes-for-google-assistant-ad-watch/</ref>\n\nThe reported fee is $250,000. The rejected poll option is TheMcRibIsBack. The 2018 picture is an Assistant advertisement.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
