        "comment": "expanded from English Wikipedia, USA Today and the Wikimedia pageviews API",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=USA Today, 14 January 2026: he spent just over a month and a half learning Russian for Ilya Rozanov. The Wikimedia pageviews API counted 133,064 views of the English article on 12 January 2026.}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Connor Storrie\n| born, English Wikipedia = 22 February 2000, Aurora, Colorado\n| raised = Odessa, Texas\n| role = Ilya Rozanov, Heated Rivalry\n| Russian, USA Today = just over a month and a half\n| pageviews, 12 January 2026 = 133,064\n}}\n\n'''Connor Storrie''' is an American actor. English Wikipedia, the page opened for the birth date, says he was born on 22 February 2000 in Aurora, Colorado, and that the family moved to Odessa, Texas, where he was raised.<ref name=\"wiki\">English Wikipedia, \"Connor Storrie,\" opened for the birth date and the early-life section. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connor_Storrie</ref> That page's birth line reads \"Born February 22, 2000 (age 26) Aurora, Colorado, U.S.\" USA Today, on 14 January 2026, calls him 25 and \"Raised in Odessa, Texas,\" which matches a birthday on 22 February, with his 26th birthday still ahead of him on 22 February 2026.<ref name=\"usa\">USA Today, 14 January 2026. https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/2026/01/14/heated-rivalry-show-who-are-connor-storrie-hudson-williams/88184454007/</ref> The birth date in this article is the Wikipedia date, cited because that page was opened.\n\n== The role ==\nWikipedia describes him as \"best known for his breakout role as Ilya Rozanov in the sports romance series Heated Rivalry (2025–present).\"<ref name=\"wikirole\">English Wikipedia on the role. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connor_Storrie</ref> USA Today says he \"plays Russian hockey star Ilya Rozanov.\" The series is \"Based on Rachel Reid's ongoing 'Game Changers' book series\" and \"made its HBO Max debut around Christmas.\"<ref name=\"usarole\">USA Today, 14 January 2026, on the part and the series. https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/2026/01/14/heated-rivalry-show-who-are-connor-storrie-hudson-williams/88184454007/</ref> The same article says he is \"speaking with a Russian accent and in many scenes, speaking in Russian entirely,\" and that \"He spent just over a month and a half learning Russian for the role.\"<ref name=\"usarussian\">USA Today on the Russian. https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/2026/01/14/heated-rivalry-show-who-are-connor-storrie-hudson-williams/88184454007/</ref>\n\n== Before the series ==\nUSA Today says that before the series he was \"waiting tables and grabbing roles in short films.\" He is \"a young inmate\" in ''Joker: Folie a Deux'' (2024) \"who attacks and ultimately kills Arthur Fleck.\" He also plays \"Liam Hauser in the 2023 coming-of-age film Riley.\"<ref name=\"usabefore\">USA Today on the earlier work. https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/2026/01/14/heated-rivalry-show-who-are-connor-storrie-hudson-williams/88184454007/</ref> On ''Today'', quoted by USA Today that day, he said: \"I wake up, get ready, go somewhere, meet cool people and I look around and I'm like, 'I've seen this for so long on TV.'\"<ref name=\"usatoday\">USA Today, quoting ''Today'', 14 January 2026. https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/2026/01/14/heated-rivalry-show-who-are-connor-storrie-hudson-williams/88184454007/</ref> The English Wikipedia filmography, on the page opened for the birth date, also lists a cameo as a Russian Spetsnaz soldier in ''For All Mankind'' (episode \"Brave New World\") and Lance Kingston in four episodes of ''Criminal Minds'' season 19.<ref name=\"wikifilm\">English Wikipedia filmography, the page opened for the birth date. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connor_Storrie</ref>\n\n== The count ==\nThe Wikimedia pageviews API, all-access and all agents, counted 133,064 views of the English article on 12 January 2026, up from 70,286 on 10 January.<ref name=\"api\">Wikimedia pageviews API, en.wikipedia, Connor Storrie, daily, 10 to 14 January 2026. https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/metrics/pageviews/per-article/en.wikipedia/all-access/all-agents/Connor_Storrie/daily/20260110/20260114</ref> The pageview count for 12 January 2026 is 133,064. The Russian was a month and a half. The sentence he gave ''Today'' is about waking up and meeting people he had seen on television.\n\n== The two ages ==\nUSA Today does not print the calendar day of his birth. It prints the age 25 on 14 January 2026, and it prints Odessa. English Wikipedia, the page opened for the date, prints 22 February 2000 and age 26, and it prints Aurora plus the move to Odessa.<ref name=\"wikiborn\">English Wikipedia birth line, the page opened for the date. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connor_Storrie</ref><ref name=\"usaage\">USA Today, 14 January 2026, on the age and Odessa. https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/2026/01/14/heated-rivalry-show-who-are-connor-storrie-hudson-williams/88184454007/</ref> A birthday on 22 February puts the 26th birthday on 22 February 2026, after the newspaper's date, which is why one page can say 25 while the other already says 26. The Russian line stays the newspaper's: just over a month and a half, for a part played with a Russian accent and, in many scenes, in Russian entirely. The waiting-tables line is that same article. The 133,064 is the pageviews API for one day, 12 January 2026, up from 70,286 on 10 January. The line from ''Today'' is about the morning he described: he wakes up, he goes somewhere, and he meets people he had seen on television.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
