        "comment": "expanded from Firstpost and Bollywood Hungama",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Hungama prints censor certificate DIL/6/10/2026-MUM and bills Ahan Shetty as Mahendra Rawat. Firstpost, one day earlier, billed him as Lt Cdr Joseph Noronha and printed a runtime of 3 hours 16 minutes.}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Border 2\n| director = Anurag Singh\n| theatrical release = 23 January 2026\n| Firstpost runtime, 22 January 2026 = 3 hours 16 minutes\n| Hungama runtime, certificate DIL/6/10/2026-MUM = 3 hours 19 minutes\n| worldwide gross, Hungama = ₹464.5 crore\n}}\n\n'''Border 2''' is a 2026 film directed by Anurag Singh, released theatrically on 23 January 2026, over the Republic Day weekend. It is a sequel to the 1997 film Border, directed by J. P. Dutta, set in the 1971 India-Pakistan war and covering the Army, the Air Force, and the Navy.<ref name=\"fp\">Firstpost, 22 January 2026. https://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/border-2-runtime-certificate-cast-advance-collection-and-all-details-13971179.html</ref> Bollywood Hungama cast page lists the status as Released and names Netflix as a streaming partner. As of 8 October 2026 it is not unreleased, and it is not a January holdover still being covered as a new release.<ref name=\"hung\">Bollywood Hungama cast page. https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/movie/border-2/cast/</ref>\n\nFirstpost, on 22 January 2026, the day before release, names the producers as Bhushan Kumar, Krishan Kumar, J. P. Dutta, and Nidhi Dutta, and the banners as T-Series Films and JP Films. The director line calls Anurag Singh \"known for films like Kesari.\"<ref name=\"fp\" />\n\n== Two runtimes ==\nFirstpost says the CBFC cleared the film U/A (13+) with no cuts and a runtime of 3 hours and 16 minutes.<ref name=\"fp2\">Firstpost, 22 January 2026, on the certificate and the runtime. https://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/border-2-runtime-certificate-cast-advance-collection-and-all-details-13971179.html</ref> Hungama censor block does not match that runtime. It lists censor date 2026/01/21, certificate number DIL/6/10/2026-MUM, runtime 3h 19min, certification U/A.<ref name=\"cert\">Bollywood Hungama, the censor block. https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/movie/border-2/cast/</ref> The Hungama certificate is dated the day before Firstpost published a CBFC runtime of 3 hours 16 minutes with no cuts. Both runtimes are in print. Neither page is set aside here.\n\n== Two names for Ahan Shetty ==\nFirstpost character line is Sunny Deol as Lt Col Fateh Singh Kaler, Varun Dhawan as Major Hoshiar Singh Dahiya, Diljit Dosanjh as Air Force officer Nirmal Jit Singh Sekhon, and Ahan Shetty as Navy officer Lt Cdr Joseph Noronha. Also named there: Mona Singh, Sonam Bajwa, Anya Singh, and Medha Rana.<ref name=\"fp3\">Firstpost, 22 January 2026, the character line. https://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/border-2-runtime-certificate-cast-advance-collection-and-all-details-13971179.html</ref> The Firstpost sentence is \"Ahan Shetty also features prominently, playing Navy officer Lt Cdr Joseph Noronha.\"<ref name=\"fp3\" />\n\nHungama cast billing for Ahan Shetty is Mahendra Rawat, not Joseph Noronha. On that page Diljit Dosanjh is billed Nirmaljit Singh Sekhon. Sunny Deol is Fateh Singh Kaler. Varun Dhawan is Hoshiar Singh. Suniel Shetty is listed as Bhairav Singh.<ref name=\"names\">Bollywood Hungama, the cast billing. https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/movie/border-2/cast/</ref> The character name for Ahan Shetty is unresolved. Firstpost says Lt Cdr Joseph Noronha. Hungama says Mahendra Rawat. The Diljit billing also differs: Nirmal Jit Singh Sekhon on Firstpost, Nirmaljit Singh Sekhon on Hungama. Firstpost gives Sunny Deol the rank Lt Col and Varun Dhawan the rank Major. Hungama prints the names without those ranks.<ref name=\"names\" />\n\n== The credits that match ==\nHungama agrees with Firstpost on director Anurag Singh, the release date 23 January 2026, the status Released, and the producers Bhushan Kumar, J. P. Dutta, Krishan Kumar, and Nidhi Dutta. Hungama lists screenplay and dialogue as Anurag Singh and Sumit Aroraa, cinematographer Anshul Chobey, editor Manish More, and background score John Stewart Eduri.<ref name=\"crew\">Bollywood Hungama, crew and status. https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/movie/border-2/cast/</ref> Hungama lists Netflix under Streaming Partners. Song composers named there are Anu Malik, Mithoon, Vishal Mishra, Sachet Tandon, Gurmoh, and Parampara Tandon.<ref name=\"crew\" />\n\n== Advances, then the Hungama gross ==\nFirstpost, citing Sacnilk before opening, says more than 1.75 lakh tickets had sold for 13,585 shows, about Rs 5.65 crore in gross advances, or about Rs 9.93 crore including block seats.<ref name=\"adv\">Firstpost, 22 January 2026, citing Sacnilk on advances. https://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/border-2-runtime-certificate-cast-advance-collection-and-all-details-13971179.html</ref>\n\nHungama box-office page lists India nett total ₹341.70 crore, opening day ₹32.10 crore, opening weekend ₹129.89 crore, and week 1 ₹244.97 crore.<ref name=\"bo\">Bollywood Hungama box-office page. https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/movie/border-2/box-office/</ref> Hungama summary line puts worldwide gross at ₹464.5 crore, India gross ₹406.79 crore, overseas ₹57.71 crore, and India nett ₹341.70 crore. The summary sentence is \"Border 2 collected ₹464.5 cr. at the worldwide box office.\"<ref name=\"bo2\">Bollywood Hungama, the worldwide summary. https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/movie/border-2/box-office/</ref>\n\nA ₹275 crore budget appeared in a Wikipedia snippet and a blog search snippet. It was not confirmed on Firstpost or Hungama, so it is not used. No Box Office Mojo dollar gross was opened. No budget is stated.<ref name=\"bo2\" /> The India nett figure on the Hungama page is 341.70 crore.\n\nThe certificate number is DIL/6/10/2026-MUM. The pages do not agree who Ahan Shetty plays.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
