        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Deadline, 21 April 2026: at the Chapel of the Bells in Las Vegas, Zendaya styled a bride and bought the gown.}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = The Drama\n| director = Kristoffer Borgli\n| U.S. release, Box Office Mojo = 3 April 2026\n| worldwide gross, Box Office Mojo = $134,670,180\n| production, Deadline = $28 million net, Square Peg\n| gown, Deadline = bought at the Chapel of the Bells\n}}\n\n'''The Drama''' is a 2026 film written and directed by Kristoffer Borgli and released in U.S. theaters on 3 April 2026 by A24. The stars on the A24 page are Zendaya and Robert Pattinson.<ref name=\"a24\">A24 film page. https://a24films.com/films/the-drama</ref> Box Office Mojo daily chart runs through 21 May 2026 and does not show an October engagement. As of 8 October 2026 the film is not unreleased, and it is not described as still in theaters.<ref name=\"mojo\">Box Office Mojo. https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl1676574721/</ref>\n\nA24 gives only this synopsis: \"A happily engaged couple is put to the test when an unexpected turn sends their wedding week off the rails.\"<ref name=\"a24\" /> Borgli site says he wrote and directed it, lists Zendaya, Robert Pattinson, Alana Haim, Mamoudou Athie, Hailey Gates, Zoë Winters, and Anna Baryshnikov, and says \"Released by A24.\"<ref name=\"borgli\">Kristoffer Borgli site. https://www.kristofferborgli.com/the-drama</ref> The A24 page and the Borgli site do not give a release date, a rating, or a budget. Those come from Mojo and from Deadline.<ref name=\"borgli\" />\n\n== The Mojo totals ==\nBox Office Mojo lists distributor A24, release 3 April 2026, MPAA R, running time 1 hr 45 min, opening $14,380,197 in 3,087 theaters, and a widest release of 3,151 theaters. Domestic is $48,102,144. International is $86,568,036. Worldwide is $134,670,180. The page splits that worldwide total as domestic 35.7 percent and international 64.3 percent.<ref name=\"mojo2\">Box Office Mojo grosses and the opening. https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl1676574721/</ref> The daily table shows Friday 3 April at $6,424,320 and marks 5 April as Easter Sunday, when the three-day opening reached $14,380,197. The Sunday figure on that row is $3,330,367.<ref name=\"daily\">Box Office Mojo daily table. https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl1676574721/</ref>\n\n== Fifth film to $100 million ==\nDeadline story of 21 April 2026 says the film had crossed $100 million worldwide that day, the fifth A24 film to do so in what Deadline calls the studio's 13-year history. Running totals in that story were about $40 million domestic and $60 million international. Those are earlier than the Mojo figures of $48,102,144 domestic and $86,568,036 international.<ref name=\"deadline\">Deadline, 21 April 2026. https://deadline.com/2026/04/the-drama-box-office-zendaya-robert-pattinson-1236867132/</ref> Deadline calls the film a \"$28M net Square Peg production,\" produced by Ari Aster, Lars Knudsen, and Tyler Campellone. It says the film beat the Challengers worldwide finish of $96.1 million. Domestic opening in the Deadline rounding is $14.3 million. Worldwide opening in that rounding is $28 million.<ref name=\"deadline2\">Deadline, 21 April 2026, on the Square Peg figure and Challengers. https://deadline.com/2026/04/the-drama-box-office-zendaya-robert-pattinson-1236867132/</ref>\n\nDeadline says A24 sold foreign rights out of Cannes the previous year. UK distributor EFD opened to $2.8 million, which Deadline calls the highest opening for an A24 production in the UK, \"not counting We Live in Time at $3.5M, a local title that A24 acquired.\" The UK cume in that story was $10.6 million.<ref name=\"uk\">Deadline, 21 April 2026, on the UK opening. https://deadline.com/2026/04/the-drama-box-office-zendaya-robert-pattinson-1236867132/</ref>\n\n== The other openings, as of 21 April ==\nOther territory figures in that Deadline story, as of 21 April 2026: France opening $1.8 million via Metropolitan, cume $5.3 million; Italy opening $1.4 million via I Wonder, cume $5.2 million; Turkey cume $832,000 via TME, called an A24 opening record there; Mexico opening $805,000 via Sun.<ref name=\"terr\">Deadline, 21 April 2026, the territory lines. https://deadline.com/2026/04/the-drama-box-office-zendaya-robert-pattinson-1236867132/</ref>\n\nDeadline audience note: women were 60 percent of the crowd and people under 35 were 80 percent, and \"80% of audiences polled by A24 said they bought tickets for both\" Zendaya and Pattinson.<ref name=\"aud\">Deadline, 21 April 2026, the audience note. https://deadline.com/2026/04/the-drama-box-office-zendaya-robert-pattinson-1236867132/</ref> Deadline calls the story \"a rather morbid topic\" and does not define it.<ref name=\"aud\" />\n\n== The chapel ==\nDeadline says the campaign included a real wedding stunt: Zendaya and Alana Haim at the Chapel of the Bells in Las Vegas in March, where Zendaya, with stylist Law Roach, styled a bride and bought the gown. The sentence is \"styled her dress and even bought the gown for her.\"<ref name=\"chapel\">Deadline, 21 April 2026, on the Chapel of the Bells. https://deadline.com/2026/04/the-drama-box-office-zendaya-robert-pattinson-1236867132/</ref> No premiere-city detail beyond that March Las Vegas stunt was confirmed on the A24 page. The Friday gross on the Mojo daily table is 6424320 dollars.\n\nShe bought the gown. The worldwide total on Mojo is $134,670,180.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
