        "daysAgo": 6,
        "comment": "expanded from Britannica, GBH, ABC News and Variety",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=GBH, 26 July 2017, quoting him: \"it was a little shire in the north where most of the people were from Ohio.\"}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Dick Van Dyke\n| born = 13 December 1925, West Plains, Missouri\n| Mary Poppins, 1964 = Bert and Mr. Dawes Senior\n| apology = BAFTA, via GBH, 26 July 2017\n| turned 100 = 13 December 2025\n| 2024 video = Coldplay, All My Love, at 98\n}}\n\n'''Dick Van Dyke''' was born on 13 December 1925 in West Plains, Missouri. The original name is Richard Wayne Van Dyke. Britannica, revised 26 September 2026, lists his age as 100.<ref name=\"brit\">Encyclopaedia Britannica, \"Dick Van Dyke,\" revised 26 September 2026. https://www.britannica.com/biography/Dick-Van-Dyke</ref> In ''Mary Poppins'' (1964) he played the dual role of street merchant Bert and bank manager Mr. Dawes Senior. GBH describes the same performance as the chimney sweep, Bert.<ref name=\"britbert\">Britannica on Bert and Mr. Dawes Senior. https://www.britannica.com/biography/Dick-Van-Dyke</ref><ref name=\"gbhbert\">GBH, 26 July 2017, on Bert. https://www.wgbh.org/news/2017-07-26/dick-van-dyke-apologizes-for-his-atrocious-cockney-accent-in-mary-poppins</ref> No performance after the 13 December 2025 birthday was on a page opened for this article, so none is stated.\n\n== The apology ==\nGBH, on 26 July 2017, quoted him after BAFTA named him for an award: \"I appreciate this opportunity to apologize to the members of BAFTA for inflicting on them the most atrocious cockney accent in the history of cinema.\"<ref name=\"gbh\">GBH, 26 July 2017. https://www.wgbh.org/news/2017-07-26/dick-van-dyke-apologizes-for-his-atrocious-cockney-accent-in-mary-poppins</ref> Asked where the accent was meant to be from, he said, in the same article: \"They ask what part of England I was meant to be from, and I say it was a little shire in the north where most of the people were from Ohio.\"<ref name=\"gbhohio\">GBH, quoting the Ohio line. https://www.wgbh.org/news/2017-07-26/dick-van-dyke-apologizes-for-his-atrocious-cockney-accent-in-mary-poppins</ref> He also named the coach. GBH, citing a 2012 ''Conan'' interview, quotes him: \"The guy who taught me was an Irishman … Pat O'Malley!\"<ref name=\"gbhcoach\">GBH, citing the 2012 ''Conan'' interview. https://www.wgbh.org/news/2017-07-26/dick-van-dyke-apologizes-for-his-atrocious-cockney-accent-in-mary-poppins</ref> The shire, on his account, was full of people from Ohio. The coach was Pat O'Malley.\n\n== The other credits ==\nBritannica lists a Tony for ''Bye Bye Birdie'' (1961), three Emmys for ''The Dick Van Dyke Show'' (1961-66), a Grammy connected to the ''Mary Poppins'' soundtrack, ''Diagnosis Murder'' (1993-2001), the Television Academy Hall of Fame in 1995, a Kennedy Center Honor in 2021, and a role in ''Mary Poppins Returns'' (2018) as Mr. Dawes Junior.<ref name=\"britcreds\">Britannica on the prizes and on Mr. Dawes Junior. https://www.britannica.com/biography/Dick-Van-Dyke</ref> The 1964 bank manager was Mr. Dawes Senior. The 2018 role was Mr. Dawes Junior.\n\n== The hundredth birthday ==\nABC News, on 12 December 2025, wrote that he \"approaches the century mark on Dec. 13.\" The line ABC prints is \"The funniest thing is, it's not enough. A hundred years is not enough. You wanna live more, which I plan to.\" The book, out that November, is ''100 Rules for Living to 100''.<ref name=\"abc\">ABC News, 12 December 2025. https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/dick-van-dyke-prepares-turn-100-im-lucky/story?id=128322788</ref> The birthday in the ABC story is 13 December 2025. He turned 100 on that date. No 2026 performance after it was opened, and none is claimed.\n\n== The barefoot video ==\nVariety, on 6 December 2024, reported that he stars in Coldplay's \"All My Love,\" directed by Spike Jonze and Mary Wigmore, \"dancing barefoot,\" and that he \"turns 99 on Dec. 13.\" His line in that story is \"Do you believe this man? He just wrote a song!\"<ref name=\"var\">Variety, 6 December 2024. https://variety.com/2024/film/news/dick-van-dyke-sings-dances-again-coldplay-music-video-1236238730/</ref> The video is December 2024. The age in that story is 98, with the 99th birthday on 13 December 2024. The next December is the hundredth. A hundred years is not enough. No later performance is stated.\n\nThe GBH article is 26 July 2017, and it holds both the apology and the shire. The shire, in his sentence, is in the north, and most of the people in it were from Ohio. The coach is not in that sentence. GBH reaches the coach by citing a 2012 ''Conan'' interview, and the name there is Pat O'Malley, an Irishman. Britannica's birth line remains 13 December 1925, West Plains, Missouri, on a page revised 26 September 2026 that already lists the age as 100. ABC is the day before the hundredth birthday. Variety is the December before that, when the birthday in front of him was the 99th, and the dancing it describes is barefoot, in a video directed by Spike Jonze and Mary Wigmore. No performance after 13 December 2025 was opened. A hundred years is not enough.<ref name=\"brit100\">Britannica, revised 26 September 2026, on the birth and the listed age. https://www.britannica.com/biography/Dick-Van-Dyke</ref><ref name=\"gbhboth\">GBH, 26 July 2017, on the apology and the shire. https://www.wgbh.org/news/2017-07-26/dick-van-dyke-apologizes-for-his-atrocious-cockney-accent-in-mary-poppins</ref>\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
