        "user": "HansardHannah",
        "daysAgo": 7,
        "comment": "expanded from the Apple press release, the Apple series page and Decider",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Apple press release, 2 April 2026: the island 40 miles off the New England coast is totally safe and completely normal, and the town has no Wi-Fi.}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Widow's Bay\n| premiere, Apple = 29 April 2026\n| finale, Apple and Decider = 17 June 2026\n| episodes = 10\n| rating, Apple series page = TV-MA\n| episodes directed by Hiro Murai = five\n}}\n\n'''Widow's Bay''' is a 2026 American series on Apple, starring Matthew Rhys. The official title punctuation is Widow's Bay, with the apostrophe. The URL slug on the Apple pages is widows-bay, without one. Apple premiered the series globally on Wednesday 29 April 2026 with two episodes and scheduled new episodes each Wednesday through 17 June 2026, with a two-episode drop on 27 May. The 10-episode season has finished that announced run. The finale date in both the Apple release and the Decider guide is 17 June 2026, before 8 October 2026.<ref name=\"apple\">Apple press release, 2 April 2026. https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/news/2026/04/take-a-trip-to-widows-bay-in-first-teaser-for-the-new-apple-original-series-starring-and-executive-produced-by-emmy-award-winner-matthew-rhys/</ref>\n\nApple release says the series was created and executive produced by Katie Dippold, who is also showrunner. Hiro Murai directed episodes and is an executive producer. Matthew Rhys is the star and an executive producer. The sentence is \"The new 10-episode series will make its global debut on Wednesday, April 29, 2026.\"<ref name=\"apple\" />\n\n== Totally safe ==\nThe setting line is a quaint island \"40 miles off the New England coast,\" which the release immediately calls \"totally safe and completely normal.\"<ref name=\"island\">Apple press release, the island line. https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/news/2026/04/take-a-trip-to-widows-bay-in-first-teaser-for-the-new-apple-original-series-starring-and-executive-produced-by-emmy-award-winner-matthew-rhys/</ref> The premise: Mayor Tom Loftis, played by Rhys, is trying to revive tourism. \"There is no Wi-Fi, spotty cellular reception,\" and locals say the island is cursed. The release as printed says \"There's no Wi-Fi, spotty cellular reception and he must contend with superstitious locals.\" Apple states that he is \"soft and cowardly. And he is.\" Tourists arrive, and \"the locals were right.\"<ref name=\"premise\">Apple press release, the premise. https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/news/2026/04/take-a-trip-to-widows-bay-in-first-teaser-for-the-new-apple-original-series-starring-and-executive-produced-by-emmy-award-winner-matthew-rhys/</ref>\n\n== The company ==\nThe lead ensemble on the Apple release is Matthew Rhys, Kate O'Flynn, Stephen Root, Kingston Rumi Southwick, Kevin Carroll, and Dale Dickey. Supporting names on that release are K Callan and Jeff Hiller. The studio is Apple Studios. The company of Murai is named Chum Films. The other executive producers are Carver Karaszewski, Claudia Shin, and Rhys.<ref name=\"cast\">Apple press release, the ensemble. https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/news/2026/04/take-a-trip-to-widows-bay-in-first-teaser-for-the-new-apple-original-series-starring-and-executive-produced-by-emmy-award-winner-matthew-rhys/</ref> Apple says Murai directs five episodes. The other directors named are Ti West, Sam Donovan, and Andrew DeYoung.<ref name=\"direct\">Apple press release, the directors. https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/news/2026/04/take-a-trip-to-widows-bay-in-first-teaser-for-the-new-apple-original-series-starring-and-executive-produced-by-emmy-award-winner-matthew-rhys/</ref>\n\n== TV-MA ==\nThe Apple series page rates it TV-MA and files it under mystery and thriller, with release date 29 April 2026. The descriptive copy repeats the 40-mile island and the \"no Wi-Fi\" line. The title on both Apple pages uses the apostrophe.<ref name=\"page\">Apple series page. https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/originals/widows-bay/</ref> The genre line on the press release is \"Blending genuine horror with character-driven comedy.\" The press-page subscription boilerplate, not specific to this show, lists Apple TV at $14.99 per month.<ref name=\"genre\">Apple press release, the genre line and the boilerplate price. https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/news/2026/04/take-a-trip-to-widows-bay-in-first-teaser-for-the-new-apple-original-series-starring-and-executive-produced-by-emmy-award-winner-matthew-rhys/</ref> No viewership number was on the Apple pages.<ref name=\"genre\" />\n\n== Titles, which are Decider titles ==\nDecider guide of 29 April 2026 says season 1 is 10 episodes and the finale is 17 June. The titles below are Decider titles. They are not printed on the Apple press pages opened. Decider lists: (1) \"Welcome to Widow's Bay!\" on 29 April; (2) \"Lodging\" on 29 April; (3) \"The Inaugural Swim\" on 6 May; (4) \"Beach Reads\" on 13 May; (5) \"What to Expect on Your Trip\" on 20 May; (6) \"Our History\" on 27 May; (7) \"Seasickness\" on 27 May; (8) \"Your Baggage\" on 3 June; (9) \"Emergency Shelter\" on 10 June; (10) \"We Hope You Enjoyed Your Time!\" on 17 June.<ref name=\"decider\">Decider episode guide, 29 April 2026. https://decider.com/2026/04/29/widows-bay-episode-guide-how-many-episodes-widows-bay-cast/</ref> Episodes 6 and 7 share 27 May, which is the two-episode date in the Apple schedule.<ref name=\"decider\" />\n\nDecider role names, which the Apple release does not spell out beyond Loftis: Stephen Root as Wyck, Kate O'Flynn as Patricia, Kingston Rumi Southwick as Evan, Kevin Carroll as Sheriff Bechir Clemons, Dale Dickey as Rosemary, Jeff Hiller as Dale, and K Callan as Ruth. Those names are Decider names.<ref name=\"roles\">Decider, the role names. https://decider.com/2026/04/29/widows-bay-episode-guide-how-many-episodes-widows-bay-cast/</ref> Decider says the island is fictional and that Apple TV \"regularly\" puts episodes up at 9:00 p.m. ET the night before the listed Wednesday. That early-drop claim is a general description on Decider. It is not a sentence in the Apple press release, and it is not confirmed by Apple for this series.<ref name=\"early\">Decider, on the 9:00 p.m. ET drop. https://decider.com/2026/04/29/widows-bay-episode-guide-how-many-episodes-widows-bay-cast/</ref> The finale title on the Decider guide is episode 10.\n\nThe island is totally safe and completely normal. There is no Wi-Fi.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
